{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>יגיד</b> — concerning the rain." "<b>רעו</b> — like תרועתו (his shouting), and it is the thunder, like וישמע יהושע את קול העם ברעה (Joshua heard the sound of the people in its shouting). Even cattle and beasts of ascent, like עלות עלי, sense it when the time of the rain's coming approaches. And people have many signs from cattle and sheep — when they lie down on their right side — and from other animals."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {1 "עלות עלי is quoted from 1 Samuel 5:12; rendered literally without resolving whether Ibn Ezra intends it as 'those that ascend upon me' or cites it for the root עלה as beast of burden/ascent."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:49.966868283Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}